docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:17:Modern web applications blend links, toolbars, rich editors, canvas surfaces, independently scrolling panes, virtualized lists, custom widgets, embedded frames, and extensive application shortcuts. The friction visible in qutebrowser discussions is not simply that these sites require typing: it is that the browser and the application often disagree about who owns a key, what has focus, which element is actionable, or where scrolling and pointer gestures should be directed. Historical qutebrowser reports are useful as failure archetypes, **not** proof every bug persists on current releases.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:19:Ferric has already implemented significant answers: validated Hints; a 3×3 recursive native Grid; explicit document-local scroll policies; transient and locked Insert; persistent Pass-through; and, in PR #9, **Pass Next Key**. The new feature forwards one real key press, repeats and release, then restores Normal; it is already bound to `Ctrl+Shift+v` and `;v`. Persistent Pass-through uses `Ctrl+v`. `Ctrl+Escape` is the designated recovery chord in both variants; `Ctrl+Shift+Escape` retains its existing emergency behaviour. Do not duplicate any of this.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:34:| Multi-pane applications | Multiple independently scrollable panes are common; focus is not reliable scroll authority | Ferric **already has** explicit scroll target; expose it alongside region actions |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:35:| Semantically opaque controls, canvas and drag-only UIs | Qutebrowser's [double-click request #446](https://github.com/qutebrowser/qutebrowser/issues/446); custom widgets and canvas limitations | Spatial Grid **already covers** point click/hover; region-scoped Grid and bounded gestures remain |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:39:Google Docs, Sheets, Slides, JupyterLab, Gmail, Discord, Slack, Trello, GitHub's rich interfaces, YouTube, diagram editors and map applications are useful **benchmark targets**, not site-specific implementation requirements. For each failure, distinguish whether it is reproduced in *current Ferric*, a hypothetical gap, or a historical qutebrowser report.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:51:| Pass-through | **Implemented.** `Ctrl+v` persistent; ordinary Escape belongs to page; `Ctrl+Escape` exits. | Consider preserving explicit persistent pass-through across same-document SPA changes after qualification |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:52:| Pass Next Key | **Implemented in PR #9.** `Mode::PassThroughOnce`, `Ctrl+Shift+v` / `;v`, actual Qt press/repeat/release, entry-key and delayed-event handling, automatic return to Normal. | No new feature; retain and regress-test during future key policy work |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:113:Keep the current `Mode::PassThrough`, `Mode::PassThroughOnce`, current bindings, original Qt events, Ctrl+Escape recovery and Ctrl+Shift+Escape emergency behaviour. Do not introduce `page-keys next`, another one-shot mode, a second native key filter, or a separate JS key-synthesis service.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:138:set = { "input.shortcut_policy" = "mixed", "input.page_keys" = ["Ctrl+Alt+m", "Ctrl+Shift+7"] }
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:141:A page-key entry must be one canonical physical key gesture, not a multi-key browser chain. Validate case, modifier combinations, representation, duplicate/collision handling, count/keychain ambiguity and current binding compatibility. **For v1, reserve `:` as the guaranteed Normal-mode command entry, plus `Ctrl+Escape`, `Ctrl+Shift+Escape` and `Ctrl+Shift+v` as required browser controls.** Reject attempts to put these in `input.page_keys` with a clear validation error. The user may still forward a literal `:` using the already-implemented Pass Next Key mode; more flexible command-entry remapping requires a separate usability/security review. Use existing binding-key canonicalization where compatible. Do not add a new arbitrary command language. `input.page_keys` should be bounded (e.g. no more than 64 entries per rule, after a test-backed schema decision), and full effective policy is resolved from the existing site-rule layering and validated atomically. The existing `input.entry_mode` and `site_rules.set` must not silently interpret these new values until their schemas are extended.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:154:- Native prompts and guaranteed rescue controls outrank per-site page mappings.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:160:`Ctrl+Escape` remains the recovery from the two explicit pass-through modes. `Ctrl+Shift+Escape` retains emergency/fullscreen behaviour. A future Mixed policy must never take away the ability to enter browser command mode or reach a documented recovery control. In v1, `:` remains browser-owned for entering commands, and `Ctrl+Shift+v` remains browser-owned for one-shot forwarding; reserve these together with both rescue chords, browser chrome focus, and all native security/permission prompt controls from page mapping. Any further reservations must be explicitly documented and test-protected, not inferred by websites.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:171:- **Same-document History API change or fragment-only URL change:** keep *user-entered persistent* Pass-through if the same document, view and owner remain; do not promote to or enable it automatically. Re-evaluate new site-rule Mixed mappings before the next new gesture.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:179:A site-configured `f`, `/`, `?` or `Ctrl+f` goes exclusively to the page; **attempting to configure `:` for page ownership is rejected in v1**, leaving Normal command entry available. No duplicate DOM key events; no accidental Normal command after async WebEngine propagation. Default/unconfigured websites behave exactly as before. Existing Pass Next Key and Insert native suites remain green.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:216:Do not create another independent page-element registry. Extend `HintKind` or introduce a thin typed target family mapped to the existing validated `HintTarget`/`HintCandidate` representation. The current `element_id`, frame path, live document identity, geometry and fresh-check boundary remain authoritative. Provider-returned capabilities must be validated by Rust, not blindly accepted from DOM JSON.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:221:- **Surface:** visual interaction areas such as canvas, video, large non-semantic widget container, iframe and embedded object. A Surface may have no inspectable child semantics.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:227:A validated region may expose `hint-within`, `search-within`, `grid-within`, and `set-scroll-target` if those actions make sense. A surface may expose `grid-within` and focus but not necessarily click or navigation. Native activation and clipboard actions remain kind- and policy-gated. Cross-origin frame contents are **not** exposed through parent DOM traversal; the parent iframe box is only a surface anchor.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:269:**Completion condition:** canvas, video and a cross-origin iframe exterior can be selected and clicked by native Grid without touching the mouse, and stale/reflowed targets reject rather than redirect.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:302:3. **Wheel/local scrolling:** only if specific benchmark cases cannot be solved through existing explicit scroll targets. Do not duplicate scroll policies.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:322:Separately assess whether public accessibility APIs expose useful roles, labels, bounds and actions for custom widgets/closed shadow implementations. Treat accessibility as a complementary provider, not an origin bypass or universal solution for canvases. No new provider is shipped until it can be independently revalidated and safely deactivated on navigation.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:330:Input key: Ctrl+f [display only if explicitly requested]
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:349:Open document → manually enter `I` for Locked Insert → edit and use real app shortcuts (`Ctrl+v` persistent or Mixed page bindings when implemented) → return to Normal → find named Share/comment controls via Hints or Page Target Search → choose document outline as region → if needed pin a specific scroll pane with `;s` → use Grid within the rendered editor for opaque visual interactions. **Do not assert rich-document editor writeback or every Docs shortcut works until live qualified.**
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:358:Focus player → `;v`, then `f` (already tested in PR #9) → resume Normal → hover Grid to reveal controls → hints/search locate captions/settings. `Ctrl+v` supports longer native player shortcut sessions.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:360:### Diagram/map canvas
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:361:Select the visual Surface → Grid within rectangle → click/hover item → only after separate native gesture qualification, bounded pan/drag/resize. Do not infer semantic canvas objects without application accessibility or adapter evidence.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:369:| `shortcut-conflicts.html` | `f`, `/`, `?` and Ctrl combinations with Ferric bindings; reserved `:` validation; exactly one owner, native down/repeat/up |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:376:| `canvas-iframe.html` | Native scoped pointer actions; same-origin and cross-origin-frame exterior |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:383:Also maintain a **dated live task matrix** on disposable profiles for Google Docs/Sheets/Slides, Gmail, JupyterLab, a Monaco and CodeMirror editor, Trello or similar, Discord/Slack, GitHub heavy views, YouTube, a map/diagram canvas and an embedded iframe tool. Distinguish actual Ferric app tests from isolated Chromium page-script and static-source tests. Record OS/compositor, Qt/WebEngine/Chromium version, page version where possible, exact task, input sequence and outcome; do not claim results not run.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:431:**WEBAPP-002** Existing `Ctrl+v`, `Ctrl+Shift+v`, `;v`, `Ctrl+Escape`, `Ctrl+Shift+Escape`, `i` and `I` retain their established behaviour unless an explicitly reviewed compatibility change is approved.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:434:**WEBAPP-005** Reserved rescue, security/prompt and native controls cannot be captured by per-site page mappings.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/sources/v02-original.md:455:Not in the initial implementation: universal “WebApp mode”; hostname-specific key-router branches; remote downloadable adapters; synthetic browser-privileged key/pointer injection; unrestricted desktop input automation; persistent DOM identity or page target lists; generic rich-editor overwrite; automatic page-owned keys inferred from untrusted DOM; fake cross-origin DOM access; arbitrary closed-shadow inspection; fully semantic canvas navigation without accessibility evidence; generalized gestures before native release cleanup qualification; virtualized offscreen document-wide target search; and broad product compatibility claims based only on synthetic tests.
