docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:35:| Capability-gated expansion | Research or implementation only where the defined evidence permits it | Double-click; in-view drag; framework writeback; child-frame/accessibility providers; alternative labels; wheel investigation |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:55:At implementation start, S00 records actual HEAD, dirty files, repository instructions, Qt/Chromium build, Rust toolchain and supported platforms. If HEAD differs from the pinned baseline, inspect the changed symbols and map equivalent APIs. Already implemented work is verified and marked as such. Do not overwrite it. No merge, reset, force push, installation, profile migration or work on the concurrent versioning branch is authorised by this pack.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:66:| Transient Enter / modified Enter | Ordinary Enter completes the transient interaction; Shift/Ctrl/Alt/Meta Enter retain the established editing behaviour; IME rules remain |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:67:| `Ctrl+v` | Persistent Pass-through from Normal; in editing contexts it retains the current page/editing meaning |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:68:| `Ctrl+Shift+v` and `;v` | Pass Next Key; do not implement another one-shot mode |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:69:| `Ctrl+Escape` | Recovery from either explicit pass-through variant |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:70:| `Ctrl+Shift+Escape` | Existing emergency/fullscreen behaviour, not a renamed recovery shortcut |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:73:| `;s`, `;S`, `scroll-target` | Existing Auto / Document / exact Element semantics |
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:107:Every asynchronous callback verifies its original owner/session/revision. A mismatch is a bounded rejection. Closing a session must not destroy a map before an accepted callback consumes it. Explicitly transfer a short-lived lease when handing a target to another local interaction, then release the source map. Long-lived scroll/scope references remain weak; nothing is persisted.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:190:First extraction is **behaviour-preserving**: use one source of helper functions, structured/JSON-encoded data arguments and the same isolated world. Do not simultaneously change to permanent per-document injection, alter world IDs or replace the Hint/scroll identity maps.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:198:Implement F-05 for the seven existing families only: `all`, `links`, `inputs`, `buttons`, `images`, `media`, `scrollables`. Regions/surfaces/proxy recognisers are not a new arbitrary selector/plugin language in this increment.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:206:Start from built-ins, then apply the existing global/profile/site/runtime precedence. At each participating family entry, `extend` appends unique strings in stable order; `replace` replaces the current list. Missing family means inherit. Site order remains the repository's existing priority/source order; do not add a different specificity algorithm. Effective `all` is its own family, not an undocumented union of every customised family. Secondary discovery passes, including implicit scrollable discovery, must honour an explicit replacement or disabled family.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:208:The selector only broadens/narrows **discovery eligibility**. It does not grant a kind, native input, focus, disabled/inert bypass, URL interpretation or new action capability. Actual type/action classification still uses the normal semantic predicates. A visible custom div matched in `all` may be represented as a generic control; it is not automatically a link/editor. Link URL operations require a real validated destination. A `scrollables` replacement still requires actual axis scrollability.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:224:Keep only `browser-first` and `mixed` in this increment. Broad page-first, wildcard key classes and per-DOM-context automatic remaps remain deferred. Mixed applies in **Normal mode only**; it does not reinterpret typing or pass-through modes.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:228:Use the repository's logical key-token representation for matching. A **native gesture identity** tracks press/repeat/release; this does not mean key mappings become physical-scancode, layout-independent bindings. AltGr, dead keys, layout changes and composition require native facts and regression tests; do not collapse AltGr into a user-written Ctrl+Alt mapping.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:237:6. Effective exact-key Mixed mapping.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:244:In Normal, `:`, ordinary `Escape`, `Ctrl+Escape`, `Ctrl+Shift+Escape` and `Ctrl+Shift+v` cannot be assigned to `input.page_keys`. Existing native security/prompt and enabled media handling also remain outside site mappings. Normal `:` remains command entry; `/`, `?`, `f`, digits and supported modified keys may be page-owned.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:246:A new gesture starts a browser keychain/count only when it is browser-owned. Once started, its continuation is browser-owned through completion, mismatch, timeout or cancellation. Never replay a buffered prefix or a rejected suffix to the page. A page mapping for `g` can make Normal `gg` unreachable before a chain starts; `binding-explain` must identify the conflict. A page mapping for a digit takes precedence over starting a count, but not over an already active browser-owned count/chain. Configuration changes cancel incomplete chains before the next new gesture; they do not retarget a held physical key.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:288:Initial **Regions**: visible main/nav/aside and named sections, dialogs, toolbars, tablists, trees, listboxes, grids, validated editor representatives, and independently scrollable panes. Initial **Surfaces**: visible canvas/video, iframe/frame exterior and object/embed elements. Do not infer arbitrary generic divs are interactive from area alone. A later evidenced adapter can declare a specific container.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:290:Chosen family cap: 256 regions and 256 surfaces, still within the existing 5,000 overall candidate limit. Ordinary semantic controls retain their existing minimum visibility policy. Unnamed purely visual surfaces require at least 16 by 16 CSS pixels; structurally named semantic regions are not excluded merely for being small. Exclude hidden buffers and offscreen canvases. Deduplicate by retained identity, not name; represent multiple eligible actions on one row where needed.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:298:Scope represents one exact selected region/surface in one live document, not a remembered CSS selector. A local handoff acquires a validated weak scope lease before ending the source Hint/Target Search map. If the supported engine cannot supply the required weak-reference behaviour, refuse the scoped handoff and offer the existing full-view Grid; do not retain a hidden strong-reference fallback. Only one active page-target interaction session per window; no simultaneous independent label authorities.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:304:A scroll-target action hands the exact element to the **existing** setter, preserving weak state, axis rules and Auto/Document distinction. Scoped Hints/Search/Grid do not themselves change scroll ownership. A cross-origin surface rejects semantic Hint/Search within and offers scoped Grid. Closed roots remain uninspected.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:317:DOM CSS pixels and Qt logical pixels must not be assumed identical at arbitrary zoom. The adapter's measured/qualified mapping owns the conversion. Do not multiply by DPR twice. Border offsets, scrolling, clipping, zoom and scale are fixtures, not guessed arithmetic.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:319:Initial semantic frame projection may reject rotated/skewed/3D transforms or unsupported mappings with `unsupported-geometry`. Do not pretend an axis-aligned bounding rectangle is an exact transform. Full-view manually aimed Grid remains available as the existing raw-coordinate fallback. Scope geometry is freshly validated and converted before entering the core.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:323:Before commit, verify owner/surface/configuration, scope validity, the captured region geometry and point containment. Chosen geometry-stability tolerance for a scoped commit: 0.5 ViewLocal logical pixel on each rectangle edge; otherwise cancel and let the user re-aim. This does not create semantic knowledge of moving canvas internals.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:325:Do not cancel on every repaint: that would make video/canvas interaction unusable. Cancel on actual observed owner/surface/geometry/scroll invalidation according to the existing policy and the scoped additions. Internal canvas animation and the JS/native interval retain C06's explicit limitations.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:359:Run 1,000 start/cancel cycles with observer/listener/map counts returning to baseline, plus dynamic-scope handoff and forced-GC tests. JS heap bytes alone are not a deterministic leak oracle; inspect retained objects/counters and report trend. Keep DevTools, when needed to force GC for tests, on disposable local qualification instances only, never as production functionality.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:377:**Double-click:** qualify public Qt event ordering and the existing adapter extension against native/DOM event counters. Provide an explicit Grid/action choice, no default key remap. Do not issue two DOM click fallbacks. Abort before delivery on invalid ownership and never repeat an uncertain transaction. Ensure one double-click does not unintentionally invoke two navigation actions through Ferric's URL path.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:385:HTML drag-and-drop, pointer capture, canvas panning and sliders must be qualified separately. Passing one pointermove fixture is not universal drag support. If a required public-API boundary fails, record a no-go and do not enable the feature. S21's implementation is conditional on S20's positive evidence.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:387:**Wheel:** retain the requested investigation but add no new wheel mode by default. A wheel-only custom widget first tries page shortcuts and existing explicit scroll targeting. Only an evidenced unsolved task can justify a separate future wheel ADR; it does not reuse or corrupt a selected DOM scroll target.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:401:**Accessibility provider:** S24 tests publicly available roles, names, bounds and actions for relevant closed/custom controls. Do not assume a canvas exposes semantic children. Preserve origin/lifecycle/privacy controls, avoid destructive actions without local intent, and demonstrate coexistence with screen readers. Until qualified, use the existing visual fallback.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:421:Manual journeys use disposable profiles and authorised test documents/accounts. Cover Docs/Sheets/Slides, Gmail, JupyterLab or a hosted advanced editor, GitHub, Reddit, Slack/Discord/WhatsApp where accessible, YouTube, Kanban, maps/diagrams and embedded viewers. Record exact URL privately when it contains a document/account token; publish a sanitised URL and reproducible task. Do not send messages, share documents, make purchases or change production data merely to complete a test.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:423:Important journeys include autocomplete Enter versus submission, page Escape, rich-text paragraphs, roving tabindex/ARIA widgets, tab/file-picker transitions, nested scrolling, input proxies, canvas controls and cross-origin exteriors. For each distinguish target fixture support, native Ferric support and live-site outcome. Authentication denial, engine version, codecs, PDF UI and permissions are separate compatibility failures, not automatically keyboard defects.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:429:Each slice has a bounded intent, source mappings, relevant contracts, allowed existing anchors/new modules, implementation order, tests, prohibitions and exit criteria. Verify actual local symbols before editing; no fictitious method calls or unreviewed replacement modules. A change outside the write scope requires a short scope-amendment record explaining the necessary call chain and preserving all contracts; architectural/behavioural changes outside this specification require the slice to stop.
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:449:The source invariants WEBAPP-001–022 are retained in the traceability map. The following unified invariants are the normative version when wording conflicts with a platform limitation:
docs/implementation/keyboard_interaction-v03/PROPOSAL.md:469:| UI-017 | Scope/search/proxy/native sessions release maps, weak leases, observers and listeners at terminal boundaries. |
